I think design from what I understand  comes a lot from the place of empathy  and understanding what the end user  needs are which is very similar in the  sense from what we do in social services  so there's a lot of synergy already in  that  the aim of this project was to design  change basically to design the change of  mindset we've come to recognize the fact  that caregivers are a blind spot for  most health and care systems around the  world if you have a caregiver that is  empower it feels confident and has the  skills to give care you can impact the  clinical outcome of a patient or other  clients so the design thinking  methodology starts by understanding of  people and we use design ethnography to  go out and spend time with people in  their everyday life so in this project  it was about going out and spending time  with caregivers we're zooming out to  understand their journeys as a whole  their life as a whole and to understand  their experiences over time this really  helped us to convey the experiences of  caregivers conveyed to the group of  people that are actually making this  change in the end the insight based  thinking helped it to be more than a  book because it f is a suite of products  that it helps at different levels from  the conceptual level in terms of being  able to understand some of the insights  in their to their films as well that  actually is very visual and helps to the  hook has to fit where there are range of  tools that would help a caregiver  understand their caregiving journey the  persona the emotions perhaps in terms of  how the topologies are as a caregiver  it's a moment for designers future  designers to to become very conscious  about the use of their skills we have a  responsibility and there is a potential  to  to social change and now is a moment for  this  [Music]
 

